{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe air in Vienna is thick with dust and music, but I am well. Tonight, the Kleins kept their word, and we sat closer to the stage than before. The Italian company performed Figaro, and I must confess, the proximity changed everything. I did not merely hear the drama; I felt the tension of the characters’ fates pressing in. Lablache’s Figaro was a whirlwind of wit, while Dardanelli’s Countess held a stillness that was almost painful to watch. The music was not just heard; it was a movement of the spirit, resolving into a freedom that felt tangible. It is a reminder that art, like the state, is the actuality of the ethical idea made visible. We are exhausted but content. The journey is long, but moments like this make the road bearable. I miss your quiet presence at home.\n\nYour devoted,\nGeorg"}}],"created":1795080320,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":192,"prompt_tokens":938,"total_tokens":1130,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-MruYkqdFiybdApaSYu9zhuWNDaArtDjz","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":938,"prompt_ms":918.798,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9795287846481876,"prompt_per_second":1020.8990441859908,"predicted_n":192,"predicted_ms":4534.061,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.738539267015707,"predicted_per_second":42.125591164300616}}